Battle for Dream Island Again (BFDIA), the second season of Battle for Dream Island, was first released on YouTube on Cary and Michael Huang's channel jacknjellify on June 30, 2012 with the episode "Yeah, Who? I Wanna Know". The season would initially end on August 2, 2013, with the release of the third season, dnalsI maerD roF elttaB, soildifying this. However, on September 1, 2023, the 6th episode would officially release, officially breaking the cancellation.
Development
Battle for Dream Island Again continued on until episode 5, which was split into five separate parts. The second part was an Adobe Flash game following Book and her team, FreeSmart, attempting to escape Evil Leafy. Episode 6 was planned to release on September 1, 2013, however it never came. Season 3, known as dnalsI maerD rof elttaB was announced on July 23, 2016, and released on September 1 of that same year. A video with BFDIA 6 deleted scenes released on August 23, 2016, and the season was officially canceled.
On August 30, 2023, a post was made stating a new episode would release on September 1, though not specifying what season. At this point, Battle for Dream Island had already finished season 4 and was on episode 6 of its 5th season, titled The Power of Two. On September 1, BFDIA 6 dropped on YouTube, ending the ten-year-long cancellation. Episodes of the season have been releasing every few months since then.
Many popular people have played guest stars throughout the season. Kevin MacLeod is a guest star in episode 12. Several guest stars have voice roles in episode 17, including Rosie O'Donnell and her child Clay O'Donnell. Rosie and Clay reprise their roles in episodes 18 and 23.
Live events in the United States
The Huang Twins have organized three live events for this season of the show, including two tours with the producers of Inanimate Insanity and a theater screening.
The twenty-third episode of the season, titled “Shattered!” was screened in Cinemark and Marcus theaters on December 1, 2025, and uploaded to YouTube the next day.
