| ShortSummary    = Leafy, with the rest of the cast in hot pursuit, escapes into Yoyleland (where previously-seen "yoyleberries" come from) using a map, which Pin rips up, rendering Leafy unable to return. Sixty-two contestants are eligible for entry into the second season, including the 20 original contestants, the 30 recommended characters from "The Reveal", and twelve additional characters: Black Hole, Bottle, Bracelety, Cake, Donut, Firey Jr., Gaty, Gelatin, Lightning, Lollipop, Puffball and Yellow Face. Twenty of these contestants qualify, as well as two chosen to automatically join, making the final total 22.
Originally, the contestants that were supposed to join were Bubble, Coiny, Firey, Flower, Golf Ball, Ice Cube, Leafy, Needle, Match, Pencil, Pin, Rocky, Spongy, Teardrop and Tennis Ball, alongside newcomers Bomby, Donut, Dora, Fries, Gelatin, Nickel and Ruby. However, since Bubble, Flower and Leafy are absent, they are disqualified and replaced with additional newcomers Book, Puffball and Yellow Face. Contestants who failed to debut are sent to the Tiny Loser Chamber.
TV, a previously recommended character, begins to host this season. Teams form, with original contestants on one team and newcomers on the other. Donut points out that his team is smaller, and, after an argument with Pencil, he chooses Match to switch. It is then revealed that one can switch teams before the challenge begins. Match switches back, and then everyone except Donut follows suit. Coiny then switches to Donut's team, and, through peer pressure, Pin switches as well. The challenge is a game of tug-of-war, which the smaller team quickly loses.
Instead of voting in the comments, viewers can like or dislike a contestant's video, with the most-liked getting to spin a prize wheel and the most-disliked getting eliminated.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = The smaller team is named W.O.A.H. Bunch, and the larger team is dubbed Team No-Name. Coiny wins the prize with 448 likes, and Donut is eliminated with 573 dislikes. The Tiny Loser Chamber, with the newly eliminated Donut, is then put inside the Locker of Losers. Coiny's prize is yoyleseeds. Teardrop is forced to switch to the smaller team, and the contest is to make "yoylestew", won by W.O.A.H. Bunch.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Puffball wins the prize with 387 likes, and Dora is eliminated with 347 dislikes. Puffball's prize is a personal speaker box, which becomes the host. Needle is forced to switch to W.O.A.H. Bunch, and the contest is to kill all of the bugs in the team's glass box, won by Team No-Name.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Teardrop wins the prize with 502 likes, though is also eliminated with 440 dislikes. Teardrop's prize was to choose between immunity into the final 15 or a "Hand-Powered Recovery Center" (HPRC), which can recover any contestant via turning a large hand crank; she chooses the HPRC. Bomby and Yellow Face switch to W.O.A.H. Bunch. The contest is to build a new Dream Island, which will be dubbed "Dream Island Again" and will be the season's prize. Team No-Name goes to Golf Ball's Underground Factory, and she uses Dream Sauce to create a magnificent new Dream Island Again. This catches the attention of Coiny, prompting him to throw Bomby into the factory and destroy the island. W.O.A.H. Bunch wins the contest, with their "Dream Island Again" being a poorly-made farm.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Pin accidentally stabs Puffball Speaker Box, resulting in Firey bringing out his personal speaker box to host. The Cake at Stake is chunks of Donut's corpse. Puffball wins the prize with 424 likes, and Match is eliminated with 426 dislikes, but Pencil saves her from being sent to the Locker of Losers. Puffball's prize is to choose which contestant should have their limbs removed, and she chooses Pin. Nickel and Spongy switch to W.O.A.H. Bunch, and Book, Ice Cube, Pencil, and Ruby make their own team, named FreeSmart. Match and Bubble, the latter of which was recovered in the previous episode, join as honorary members. The contest is to get to the summit of the far away Yoyle Mountain, in Yoyleland.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = This part of the episode is a puzzle-platform game using Adobe Flash.}} The FreeSmart members, trapped inside Evil Leafy (a red, hostile version of Leafy introduced earlier) after the events of BFDIA 5a, traverse through and escape her body using different abilities.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = After the events of BFDIA 5b, Book and Ruby successfully escape Evil Leafy, with the other FreeSmart members including Bubble and Match missing or dead. W.O.A.H. Bunch falls into the "Evil Canyon", so Coiny says Spongy should jump onto the spikes at the bottom so the other team members can land onto him. The remaining FreeSmart and W.O.A.H. Bunch members meet up and the Firey Speaker Box brings out a "Hand-Powered HPRC creator". They crank the handle until the HPRC is created.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = The FreeSmart and W.O.A.H. Bunch members are still cranking even after 78 days. Finally, an HPRC comes out, and they recover their dead team members. W.O.A.H. Bunch also recovers Puffball, so they can make her fly them to Yoyleland. This fails and they get frozen with "Freeze Juice".
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Team No-Name is flying over Davidland, an area consisting of thousands of David clones, on Puffball. Meanwhile, FreeSmart is in their personal van, the FreeSmart Supervan, at Yoyleland, and they arrive at Yoyleland's signature landmark, the abandoned but well-preserved Yoyle City. Ruby accidentally glues the Hand-Powered Recovery Center to the ground, and Pencil gets trapped by a fish's tongue. FreeSmart uses a saw to kill her, and they recover her using the Hand-Powered Recovery Center. FreeSmart and Team No-Name get to Yoyle Mountain, where they are met by the Firey Speaker Box. FreeSmart gets to the summit first. Firey Speaker Box realizes that Match isn't in the TLC, so he sends her there. While Team No-Name is about to reach the summit, Puffball betrays her team members by dropping them to be eaten by the fish. W.O.A.H. Bunch reaches the summit, which means Team No-Name loses the contest.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Puffball is eliminated at Cake at Stake. Before the challenge, Rocky, who was on Team No-Name, is convinced to switch to W.O.A.H. Bunch, much to the former team's dismay. The challenge is to find a suitable place for the team members to have a good nights' sleep. The challenge results in team W.O.A.H. Bunch being unable to sleep due to being chased by Evil Leafy for the entire night.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Ruby catches a Yoylite meteorite, which is coveted by Tennis Ball and Golf Ball for its rarity and power. Rocky is eliminated at Cake at Stake. The challenge is to build a replacement for the Tiny Loser Chamber which will be used to store the future eliminated contestants, as the current Tiny Loser Chamber (with all of the failed debuters and eliminated contestants inside it) is locked with no way to open it. Tennis Ball instructs Firey and Gelatin to switch to FreeSmart for one challenge in order to get the Yoylite. As a result, FreeSmart loses the challenge due to Firey and Gelatin not telling them what the challenge is. The one surviving replacement for the TLC is a rather shoddy-looking structure, dubbed the Weak Trembling Fortress (WTF). Rocky is placed in the WTF.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Firey is eliminated at Cake at Stake and sent to the WTF. As a result, Firey Speaker Box becomes too sad to host. Puffball Speaker Box is brought back to host. The challenge is to paint a replica of the Eiffel Tower. W.O.A.H. Bunch loses due to Gelatin giving glasses to Puffball Speaker Box which makes her see W.O.A.H. Bunch's paint color, purple, as yellow.
Note: Zach Kornfeld guest stars in this episode.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
, ,  &
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Nickel is attempting to scrub pink paint off himself. Ice Cube mentions that, being pink, she is now technically a strawberry milk cube. After Ruby recovers herself, she chomps on Ice Cube, and because Ice Cube was covered in lead paint, Ruby vomits it out. The lead paint vomit then begins corroding the Eiffel Tower. The Cake at Stake starts in FreeSmart's "Total Clubhouse of Awesomeness" at the top of the tower, with the prize being a paper airplane ticket out of the clubhouse, and Yellow Face is eliminated after Purple Face, his nemesis, steals his win tokens. The challenge is a time-based game of charades, where contestants have to answer correctly before their teammate is crushed by a trash compactor. Team No-Name is out due to them running out of players first. Contestants who were killed are sent to the underworld, where they are turned into realistic versions of themselves, though they are eventually recovered and turned back later on.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
, ,  &
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Gelatin is eliminated at Cake at Stake and sent to the WTF. Amazed by Ice Cube's "beautiful face" (her rapidly moving her tongue), almost all of the contestants, sans Fries, switch to FreeSmart, now called the "Beautiful Face Devotion Institute". The challenge is to sell the most ice cream before the first snowflake of winter arrives. Fries wins the challenge.
Note: Zach Kornfeld and TomSka guest star in this episode.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
, ,  &
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Ice Cube gets the challenge reward, which is to remove a contestant's face of her choice. Ice Cube chooses Pin, effectively rendering her completely insentient. Spongy gets eliminated, but not before accidentally killing Puffball Speaker Box. Golf Ball causes the Beautiful Face Devotion Institute to divide, with everyone returning the teams to what they were before "Taste the Sweetness". Flower, who was recovered, hosts this episode, making the challenge to remove the most petals off of her head. W.O.A.H. Bunch wins the challenge and FreeSmart goes up for elimination.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
, ,  &
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Ruby gets the challenge reward (a shrink ray), choosing to shrink Pin to the size of a real-world pushpin. Ice Cube is eliminated and sent to the WTF. Needle is forced to switch to FreeSmart and Fries goes solo once more. Since Spongy was too heavy to be launched to the WTF, he ends up crushing Flower. A swarm of bugs replace her and host the next challenge, "Bug-filled Dodgeball Insanity". Ruby finds her thirty-five sisters hiding in a bug hive, who reveal their resentment towards her as she was the only one among them to join BFDI. All 36 decide to compromise by joining the game as "Ruby". FreeSmart wins the challenge and immunity.
Note: Kevin MacLeod guest stars in this episode.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
,  &
| WrittenBy       = ,  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = The four members of the WTF leave the area to visit and explore Yoyle City, encountering various pieces of technology. Coiny digs to the underworld in an attempt to restore Pin to her full self, but ultimately fails to pull her back up. Interactions between the TLC inhabitants are shown throughout, including a call to buy five islands. Firey revives Leafy with the Recovery Center, unbeknownst to her.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
}}
| DirectedBy      = , ,  &
| WrittenBy       = ,  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = The Cake at Stake is started by the bugs, but FreeSmart kills them using Spongy, so the TLC inhabitants host the next challenge. With the help of Coiny, Pin regains her face and size as a reward. However, she does not get her limbs back, instead receiving a cable-powered mech suit. Golf Ball is eliminated and sent to the WTF. The challenge is to get to a bunk bed at the top of the TLC inhabitants' islands, in which they have missions assigned to complete in order to pass to the next island, though Evil Leafy is in pursuit. On the final island, which is to sing a song so as to impress Puffball, "Ruby", who is teamed with Book, secretly records Pin's song, modifies it, and plays it into the microphone. Having had enough of the disrespect she endured from FreeSmart in the past episodes, Pin sends a surge of electricity through her cable, which travels up the central beam and strikes "Ruby" and Book, putting them up for elimination.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
, ,  &
| WrittenBy       = , ,  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Ruby is eliminated and sent to the WTF, though her sisters also have to be sent as well. The final nine are temporarily divided into three new teams of equal size: The Hearts, The Stars, and The Quasi-Rhombicosidodecahedrons. Each team competes to get all of their respective team members inside of a birdhouse lined with lead paint. The cast eventually ends up shrinking eachother and the birdhouse down to the atomic level. The Hearts win by using lead atoms to stun the other teams.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       = ,  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Balloony ties up the rest of the TLC inhabitants and declares himself host. Bomby is eliminated and sent to the WTF. As Needle's allegiance is split between conflicting alliances, she decides to play for both teams simultaneously. In the challenge, the contestants are tasked with hiding a cherished item and seeking out their competitors' trinkets in order to tag them.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
&
| WrittenBy       = ,  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = After the contestants try to use Spongy to destroy the TLC, Balloony drives it away. The residents of the WTF take over hosting duties, including Pencil after she was eliminated at the Cake at Stake ceremony. The challenge is for the contestants be their "truest selves" (return to their typical appearance). Book embarks on a wild goose chase of errands to restore her original cover, while Tennis Ball and Nickel are sent forward in time after a mishap involving Yoylite. W.O.A.H. Bunch wins the challenge and immunity as well as Fries whose prize was immunity into the final 6.
Note: Several guest stars have voice roles in this episode, including Rosie O'Donnell and her child Clay O'Donnell.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Tennis Ball uses his challenge reward to forcibly dissolve W.O.A.H. Bunch, and Needle decides to "win for herself", effectively ending the team phase, and Nickel is eliminated. The challenge is to be the first to illuminate three beacons in their dedicated color; in the end, Pin betrays Coiny and wins immunity, though it is shown later that Coiny is indifferent to this.
Note: Rosie and Clay O'Donnell reprise their guest roles in the episode's cold open.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Fries is eliminated at the Cake at Stake ceremony. A fish monster from the sea becomes the new host of the competition, as players are tasked to fill their baskets with unique items. The episode concludes in the midst of the challenge and prompts viewers to vote on the game's next host.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Continuing after the events of the previous episode, this time the contestants must give away their ten items for immunity tickets. Needle has an advantage due to winning the first part, and Coiny and Pin end up being up for elimination after the former sacrifices himself.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       =
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = Leafy and Pin play at the park, and Leafy tries convincing Pin to help find a yellow tomato, in which they climb up a giant beanstalk which catches fire, then spin a prize wheel to get the tomato. During this, the Cake at Stake is started, with the TLC's inhabitants revealing the votes for the new hosts, which ends up being Leafy. Leafy goes to recover Firey, but Firey denies ever meeting Leafy, calling her a stranger, then walking away and disappearing, leaving Leafy saddened.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =
| ShortSummary    = The eliminated contestants rebuild the Goiky Highway, which connects the mainland to Yoyleland. Leafy is sitting next to the Hand-Powered Recovery Center when she is dropped a letter from the TLC's inhabitants confirming she's the next host. Pin is eliminated and the challenge is to travel with Leafy until she runs out of "Friendship Flags", which she places if she likes a location they visit. The contestants find a hole in the highway shaped like Woody, and Needle uses a magnet to attract the Hand-Powered Recovery Center there. Woody is recovered and slotted into the hole, later slipping and falling into a crack in the Earth that was formed from Leafy's flag planting. Tennis Ball finds out Leafy actually has millions of flags, so he starts destroying them to speed the contest up. Meanwhile, Pin is being chased by the eliminated contestants, and she uses her mech suit to erode most of Dream Island Again, leaving only a small fragment remaining. Pin saves Woody and gives him her mech suit, but dies in the process. Coiny and Needle jump into the hole with Leafy to get the last Friendship Flag. Tennis Ball gets Pin's now-discarded drill and drops it into the hole to kill Needle, Book jumps to save her but is burnt to death, and Leafy gets hit by the drill. Woody plants the flag on the show's prize.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
| WrittenBy       =  &
| OriginalAirDate =  before being released on YouTube the following day.}}
| ShortSummary    = Woody flees with the show's prize, overheating the mech suit by stuffing it with sand to create a glass bridge. Coiny is eliminated at Cake at Stake. The contest is to get to the end of the bridge and step on what's left of Dream Island Again, doing challenges based on the season's previous contests along the way. All of the challenges are optional, though advantages will be given to those who complete them by each challenge's respective eliminated contestant (Donut for the first challenge, Dora for the second, and so on). Book, Needle and Tennis Ball continually alternate between who is in the lead, culminating in a standoff between Woody and the three contestants at the end of the bridge. Woody inadvertently falls off, and Coiny uses Pin's drill to break the bridge, sending everyone and Dream Island Again falling back to the ground. Ultimately, Book becomes the final contestant to earn immunity (as well as her first victory overall), leaving Tennis Ball and Needle up for elimination.
Note: Clay O'Donnell, Rosie O'Donnell, and TomSka reprised their guest roles.
| LineColor       = FFA500
}}
